2. Round 2 finding (a) — no red evidence — CLEARED, and verified by
   reproduction rather than by reading the logs
---------------------------------------------------------------------
Six reds exist (ci/reds/W-022/01..06.log), all `# exit: 1`, all
assertion-level FAIL lines, no two identical after header strip.

A red is only evidence if a broken implementation produces it. I mutated
the implementation four ways and ran all six behaviours under each
(script $TMPDIR/mutate-w022.sh, `git checkout --` restore in an EXIT trap;
`git status --porcelain` empty afterwards):

  A  isModuleLoadFailure -> return false
  B  isModuleLoadFailure -> return true
  C  isDuplicateRed      -> return false
  D  isDuplicateRed      -> return true

Every recorded red is byte-identical to a line one of those mutations
produces, and each behaviour dies under at least one mutation:

  red 01  FAIL  same body after header = duplicate     false   <- C
  red 02  FAIL  different body = not duplicate         true    <- D
  red 03  FAIL  ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND detected          false   <- A
  red 04  FAIL  import SyntaxError detected            false   <- A
  red 05  FAIL  assertion failure not flagged          true    <- B
  red 06  FAIL  empty body not flagged                 true    <- B

Unmutated, all six PASS. So the suite bites on both exported functions in
both directions (false negative and false positive), which is more than the
one mutation qa §2 requires. The reds are the shape a stubbed/broken
implementation emits — not passing runs re-labelled, which is what round 2
warned against.

Provenance of the mutation, checked rather than taken on trust:
  $ git log --oneline -S "MODULE_LOAD_RE" --all
  $ git log -p --all -S "const MODULE_LOAD_RE" -- packages/cli/src/rules/evidence.ts
Exactly one definition has ever been written, in ea4c2dd, and it is the
regex at HEAD. No commit anywhere carries a mutated MODULE_LOAD_RE.

